        "cooked": "<p>They mentioned Schmonan, but they didn’t say Schiwng Schwong, which is what Extremeeverse Nexus Primalis should resemble, especially the middle act of the 2005 movie.</p>\n<p>Oh, and you want a painfully bad Xtremeverse?  Southwest Sentinels.  They’re all extreme cringey stereotypes.  Doc Medico is gayer than Pluck and the Village People in one, Mainstay is all tattoos and piercings and the worst biker stereotypes*, Writhe is all Gothy for no reason, and Idealist literally imagines herself a princess.  Boom, there you go.  Somebody go draw that.</p>\n<p>They said Dawn would have brown hair, but the cover is clearly a redhead.  I’m surprised they never mentioned KNYFE.  I wonder if our KNYFE might be Xtremeverse Paige Huntley.</p>\n<p>I wonder if Citizen Frost has ice wings, an ice hammer and shield, or both.</p>\n<p>Xtremeverse Count Barzakh?</p>\n<p>Mainstay* -  Oh, that’s hilarious, he’s got a Confederate Flag tattoo, which is so stupid for a guy from Arizona whose best friend is a gay Mexican.  And Doc has a  sombrero as part of his energy body.  It’s such a massive self- own, it’s almost not bad anymore!</p>\n<p>Ah, the Guise letters, I’ve missed those.  I think Xtremeverse Guise IS the body horror Guise they talked about here.</p>\n<p>Hotblack Desatio needs to weigh in on the loudest Rebel Yell question.</p>\n<p>I’m glad they abandoned the metal mask, but less so about the gear not being there.</p>",
